properties.decision:
An opposing CONTRADICTS, whether an objection in an argument or a counterexample, counts against its target by the objection's OWN computed truth:
- one that HOLDS refutes the target: the target fails, and every step resting on it is reported broken;
- one that is UNKNOWN (raised, neither established nor answered) leaves the target unknown: contested, with proof status `contested`;
- one that FAILS (answered by a reply that holds, or rejected) no longer counts.
A reply is recorded the way the objection was: a CONTRADICTS from the reply to the objection. A circle of objections (A against B, B against A) with nothing else to settle it has no verdict: both read unknown.
